 "finding": "Verdict CONFIRMED empirically: 0 of 81 audited alleles have a full-rank additive design (median rank deficiency 128 of 301 params). Prop 1s identifiability condition does not hold on the observed IEDB design for ANY allele - per-position amino-acid coverage is too sparse. Consequence (now stated in the paper): the additive PSSM baseline is only estimable under ridge regularization, so \"deep model vs additive baseline\" comparisons are against a regularized approximation, and the identifiability propositions stay conditional. This is a locked finding, reported as-is."
